{%- comment -%}
  Renders the label that goes inside a sale badge: the real discount worked
  out from compare-at vs price, e.g. "45% off", instead of a flat "Sale".

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} the product (required)
  - variant: {Object} a specific variant (optional). Pass this on the product
      page, where the shopper has picked a variant and the badge should track
      that pick. Omit it on cards, where no variant is selected yet.

  Behaviour:
  - One variant given      -> that variant's discount, e.g. "45% off"
  - No variant, all equal  -> the shared discount, e.g. "45% off"
  - No variant, mixed      -> "Up to 45% off" using the largest discount,
                              which is what "up to" actually promises
  - Nothing computable     -> falls back to the stock "Sale" label, so a badge
                              never renders empty or with a wrong number

  Percentages are floored, never rounded up: a 44.6% discount prints as 44%.
  Rounding up would advertise a bigger discount than the shopper gets.

  Prices are integers in cents, so the numerator is multiplied by 100.0 to
  force float division before flooring — plain integer division would
  truncate to 0 first.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign pct_min = 101
  assign pct_max = 0
  assign counted = 0

  if variant != nil and variant != blank and variant.compare_at_price > variant.price
    assign numerator = variant.compare_at_price | minus: variant.price | times: 100.0
    assign pct_max = numerator | divided_by: variant.compare_at_price | floor
    assign pct_min = pct_max
    assign counted = 1
  elsif product != nil
    for v in product.variants
      if v.compare_at_price > v.price
        assign numerator = v.compare_at_price | minus: v.price | times: 100.0
        assign v_pct = numerator | divided_by: v.compare_at_price | floor
        if v_pct < pct_min
          assign pct_min = v_pct
        endif
        if v_pct > pct_max
          assign pct_max = v_pct
        endif
        assign counted = counted | plus: 1
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}

{%- if counted > 0 and pct_max > 0 -%}
  {%- if pct_min == pct_max -%}
    {{- 'products.product.percent_off' | t: percent: pct_max -}}
  {%- else -%}
    {{- 'products.product.percent_off_up_to' | t: percent: pct_max -}}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- else -%}
  {{- 'products.product.on_sale' | t -}}
{%- endif -%}
